		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3905&amp;p=30343#p30343"><![CDATA[
I can confirm that it is the "Safe Pwr-on" option that triggers this behaviour. I noticed this happening a couple of weeks ago, but eventually decided it wasn't an unreasonable side effect of selecting "Safe Pwr-on" (I've only just started using this option), so I didn't bother raising it as a bug.<br><br>As stated by W3ATH, the clue is that if you watch carefully you can see a flash of life as the radio begins the reboot, and then it encounters the Safe Pwr-on flag and quits the boot process. <br><br>This seems sensible to me as it preserves, and is in compliance with, the settings that were present prior to whatever update has just been made.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4176">ZL2MGS</a> — Sun Mar 24, 2024 11:11 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
