		<published>2024-03-24T00:33:13</published>
		<id>http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3905&amp;p=30338#p30338</id>
		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3905&amp;p=30338#p30338"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: CPS R2024.03.09.01 Radio Shut Down?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3905&amp;p=30338#p30338"><![CDATA[
I figured out the problem.  However, first I need to clarify what the problem was.  It wasn't an FW issue.  It had to do with the CPS writing the CP to the radio.<br><br>There was a coincidence of events that made the shut down occur.  I got the latest CPS software and used it AFTER I'd changed a setting on the radio to "Safe Pwr-On".  What that does is require you to hold the SK1 button (above PTT) while powering on the radio.  This prevents accidental (e.g., in a backpack) turning on of the unit.<br><br>If you watch the UV-890 screen when you write a CP to it, the radio flashes off/on at the end of the write process. I turned OFF the "Safe Pwr-On" mode and the new CPS behaves normally - after writing to the radio, the radio flashes off then immediately back on.  Turn on the "Safe Pwr-On" and it can't because you're not holding that SK1 key when it tries to turn on.<br><br>So, nothing wrong with CPS, just a quirk caused by a radio setting.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5794">W3ATN</a> — Sun Mar 24, 2024 12:33 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
