<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Strange, can you power off a 390 via the green button?<br>I have always used the volume/on-off switch and press sk1 + PTT when powering on radio in DFU mode.</div></blockquote>Ah.<br><br>I was confused, I thought this problem was on the MD9600 but I see now its the 390<br><br>The ability to reboot back into the firmware is not supported by the official loader but we found a way to do this with the OpenGD77 firmware loader<br><br>Howeever in this case, it sounds like for whatever reason the bootloader in the radio is not supporting reboot after installation.<br><br>The only thing which potentially could have caused this would be a Windows update, changing something in the .Net framework or the STM DFU driver<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Mar 23, 2024 1:26 am</p><hr />
