		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3905&amp;p=30317#p30317"><![CDATA[
I just checked and I'm pretty sure its because the radio was turned off before entering DFU mode<br><br>i.e If you turn off the radio from the green button on the front panel<br>Then turn off the PSU<br>Then hold Orange and P1 to enter DFU , and while still holding Orange and P1, turn on the PSU... The radio will power on and enter DFU mode<br>Then load the firmware<br>The radio will now reboot, but becuase the previous state prior to turning on the PSU with Orange and P1 held in.... Was OFF<br><br>Then the firmware will be in its OFF state<br><br><br>The confusion is proabbly becuase this radio is never actually OFF.<br><br>There is no power control circuity in this radio. When the radio appears to be off, its only every actually in Standby. The CPU is still running, albeit in a low current standby mode.<br><br>This is the same as the official fimware<br><br>You can tell that the radio is never truely off, even with the official firmware, becuase if you measure the current when the radio is "OFF" you'll find its not 0 (zero)<br>I forget how much current the radio takes when its in standby, its a few milliamps, possibly 10 or 15mA , I can't remember the exact value.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Mar 22, 2024 8:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
